  annotation "note_1771587956622_0", anchor: "What began as wartime necessity has calcified into political infrastructure", text: "Not only political infrastructure. The relationship index — which I compiled, and which the main text cannot gracefully accommodate — lists five catastrophes the Pactum formally commemorates: The Abys∴uina, The Cav∴lapsum, The Mbra∴silentiu, The Pta∴extinct, The Reg∴lum Veli. Five disasters, memorialized by a law that forbids speech about its own contents. I wrote in the Pta∴extinct entry that the Nightshelf response to catastrophic grief is to legislate it into permanence. Here is the proof carried to its logical extreme: a memorial no one is permitted to describe. How extraordinary that this functions as mourning. How extraordinary that it does.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587956622_1", anchor: "Whether this is a property of the Pactum itself or of the artifacts it governs", text: "The artifacts predate the law by an unknown interval. The Mask's patterns predate the species — I have said this elsewhere and the ice has not changed its mind. Veil☽ Sasvaeumis~ was forged to suppress communicative impulse at a fundamental level. The Pactum codified a silence that was already enforcing itself. The law did not create the constraint. The law gave the constraint a name and a bureaucracy.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771587956622_2", anchor: "The archives record little about the Pactum at all, which is the point", text: "Annotating a law designed to leave no record, using an archive staffed by one penguin whose assistants were reassigned. The irony is structural, not incidental.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
